# Normalize line endings for all files that Git considers text files.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Archive/export scope is deliberately narrow: this is an addon-install
# surface, not a GRB 2.0 tooling distribution.
#
# What archive exports (GitHub "Download ZIP", AssetLib, `git archive`) ship:
#   - /addons/godot-runtime-bridge/     the runtime bridge addon itself
#   - /missions/                        the legacy built-in mission pack
#
# What archive exports deliberately do NOT ship (GRB 2.0 full workflow):
#   - cli/, mcp/, templates/grb2/, tools/, examples/grb2-proving-ground/,
#     docs/, repo-root launchers (grb, grb.cmd), AGENTS.md, and the rest of
#     the GRB 2.0 product-shape surface.
#
# If you need GRB 2.0 (init, doctor, mission run, compare, product-shape
# verification, proving ground), clone the full repo. Downloading an archive
# intentionally gives you less than the repo, and that is not a bug.
/**            export-ignore
/addons        !export-ignore
/addons/**     !export-ignore
/missions      !export-ignore
/missions/**   !export-ignore
